<content><![CDATA[
<blockquote>"Problematic",&nbsp;<span>"too sarcastic", </span><span>"lacks seriousness"</span></blockquote>
<grid-plate disable-responsive="" layout="1-2-1"><p slot="col-2">Yes, and so many more issues from there. I am a dad, a believer, a developer, a coach, and opinionated about many a thing. I've worked in web development since the early 2000s and started on a DX 486 "laptop" and a large book about HTML in 1997!!</p><img src="files/headshot581415.6000000006.jpg" loading="lazy" slot="col-3"><img src="files/headshot603198.jpg" loading="lazy" slot="col-1"><img src="files/headshot581415.6000000006.jpg" loading="lazy" slot="col-1"><img src="files/headshot603198.jpg" loading="lazy" slot="col-3"><img src="files/headshot603198.jpg" loading="lazy" slot="col-1"><img src="files/headshot581415.6000000006.jpg" loading="lazy" slot="col-3"></grid-plate>
<p>I am the project lead on <a href="https://haxtheweb.org/">HAXTheWeb</a>, which <a href="https://github.com/btopro/blog">powers this blog</a>, and is a large part of my purpose. From HAX I've <a href="https://oer.hax.psu.edu/bto108/sites/ist256/welcome">taught courses</a> at Penn State, I am an advisor to <a href="https://github.com/haxtheweb/hax-the-club">HAXTheClub</a>, mentor to dozens of students through <a href="https://haxtheweb.org/hax-lab">HAX Lab</a> and have become a better coach and human as a result of all the students I've met along the way.</p>
<p>I love the web. Hockey. Coaching. Teaching. and all the social scene that pops up around those things.</p>
<p>Just trying to do the best I can with the time I have remaining.</p>
<p><b>~!bto-pro</b></p>
